# site — Server Environment Variables (dev)
# Copy to .env.server and fill in required values.
# Used by: npm run dev (local development), which loads it with node's --env-file.
#
# This module is the execution layer. It holds no identity store — hq issues
# tokens and site verifies them — so there are no auth secrets here. Its one
# stored secret, its credential to hq, is encrypted with SECRETS_MASTER_KEY.

# ── Port ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The one port the site listens on, for its agents' endpoints and /health.
# Chosen to avoid clashing with hq, which uses 4100 (client) / 4101 (server).
PORT=4201

# ── Secrets at rest ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECRETS_MASTER_KEY — 32-byte base64 key this site encrypts its stored hq
# credential with, so a read of the site's database alone yields nothing that
# works. This site's own key, not hq's. REQUIRED to connect to hq: without it
# the site cannot pair or register. Losing or changing it makes the stored
# credential unreadable — the default site then re-pairs from HQ_PAIRING_SECRET
# at its next start, and any other site registers again.
# Generate: openssl rand -base64 32
SECRETS_MASTER_KEY=

# ── Registering with hq ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Register once, with the site running:  npm run site -- register <hq-url>
# It prints a code for an hq admin to approve at <hq>/sites/approve. There is
# no registration setting here for that flow — registration needs both the
# machine and an hq admin (ADR-0064), and a value in a file proves neither.
#
# HQ_URL + HQ_PAIRING_SECRET — how this site connects to hq's default site with
# no registration: the same HQ_PAIRING_SECRET as hq/.env.server. In development
# scripts/dev/pair.sh (run by the start tasks) writes both, so leave them to it.

# ── Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Points at the site-db service in the root docker-compose.yml dev stack,
# published on 127.0.0.1:4209. Start it with:
#   docker compose up -d       (from the repo root)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://agenthix:agenthix@localhost:4209/agenthix_site

# ── Runtime — agent execution (plan 5d-2) ─────────────────────────────────────
# The execution runtime lives here now: containers, MCP, git credential serving,
# run/transcript storage. hq never reads or writes this site's disk at all — it
# names a location by its owner and asks the site that holds it over the
# control channel (see hq/.env.server.example).
#
# SITE_ROOT — agent workspaces, files homes and task directories root.
# MISSING THIS FAILS SILENTLY: the runtime still boots — no error names
# SITE_ROOT — it just operates against an empty directory (observed live during
# the 2026-08-16 walkthrough: the runtime had moved here but its env hadn't).
# Always set it explicitly; never rely on the code's own fallback default.
SITE_ROOT=~/.agenthix.dev

# AGENT_CONTAINER_ISOLATION — set to true to run agents in Docker containers.
#                             Unset or false runs them as local subprocesses (dev).
AGENT_CONTAINER_ISOLATION=true

# SITE_AGENT_URL — where an agent container reaches this site's /mcp and
#                  git-credential endpoints (ADR-0066). Not this site's public
#                  address: a deployed site has none, and agents reach it over
#                  their own network by container name. Optional: defaults to
#                  http://<SITE_CONTAINER_NAME>:<PORT> in a container, else
#                  http://host.docker.internal:<PORT> under container
#                  isolation, else http://localhost:<PORT>.
# SITE_AGENT_URL=

# SITE_CONTROL_SOCKET — path to the Unix socket the local `agenthix-site`
#                       command dials. Optional: defaults to
#                       <SITE_ROOT>/run/control.sock; the Docker image sets it
#                       to /run/agenthix-site/control.sock.
# SITE_CONTROL_SOCKET=

# AGENT_NETWORK_RANGE — IPv4 range each agent container's isolated network
#                       draws a /29 from (ADR-0066). Optional: defaults to
#                       10.213.0.0/16.
# Dev uses 10.212.0.0/16 (ADDRESS_BLOCKS.devAgents in core/src/ports/ports.ts), apart from every installation's agents.
AGENT_NETWORK_RANGE=10.212.0.0/16

# HOST_NAMESPACE               — the install's namespace, which the host service
#                                sets. Agent containers are named
#                                <namespace>-agent-…, labelled <namespace>.<key>
#                                and grouped as the project <namespace>-agents.
#                                Default agenthix-dev. Every container and
#                                network a site makes also carries its own site
#                                id (<namespace>.site), and a site removes only
#                                what carries it. A second development site on
#                                the same Docker sets its own namespace here
#                                (for example agenthix-dev2), so its container
#                                names differ from the first's too.
# AGENT_CONTAINER_MEMORY       — per-container memory limit passed to
#                                `docker run --memory`. Default 8g. Any docker
#                                size (512m, 2g, a byte count).
# AGENT_CONTAINER_PIDS_LIMIT   — per-container process-count limit
#                                (`--pids-limit`, which counts threads).
#                                Default 4096. Whole numbers.
# AGENT_CONTAINER_CPUS         — per-container CPU ceiling (`--cpus`), in
#                                cores; fractions allowed. Default 2.
#                                A container belongs to one person (or the
#                                project) in one storage location, and their
#                                runs in it run at the same time — so these
#                                three are sized for several harness processes
#                                at once, up to AGENT_MAX_CONCURRENT_RUNS.
#                                Unusable or <= 0 falls back to the default: an
#                                empty value (what compose interpolates for an
#                                unset variable) would otherwise reach docker,
#                                which refuses it and fails every agent run.
# AGENT_CONTAINER_ENDRUN_SECONDS — how long the end-of-run work
#                                may take before it is abandoned. Default 30. It runs while the run
#                                still holds a concurrency slot, so a wedged
#                                container must not park it indefinitely. Work abandoned
#                                this way makes the next run recreate the
#                                container rather than reuse it.
# AGENT_CONTAINER_IDLE_MINUTES — a session container with no live run and no
#                                activity for this long is removed; the next
#                                run recreates it and the conversation resumes.
#                                Default 30. Non-numeric or <= 0 falls back to
#                                the default (never disables the sweep).
# AGENT_SESSION_IDLE_MINUTES   — a conversation with no turn running for this
#                                long is released: every process it started
#                                in its container is ended, its harness lets go
#                                of it, and its staged files are removed. It
#                                stays resumable; its next turn starts without
#                                them. A preview held open for it keeps it.
#                                Default 30. Non-numeric or <= 0 falls back to
#                                the default.
# AGENT_MAX_CONCURRENT_RUNS    — how many agent runs this site executes at once,
#                                across every container. Default 5. Whole
#                                numbers; unusable or <= 0 falls back to the
#                                default. Runs beyond it wait for a slot; turns
#                                of one conversation always run one at a time.
# HOST_NAMESPACE=agenthix-dev
# AGENT_MAX_CONCURRENT_RUNS=5
# AGENT_CONTAINER_MEMORY=8g
# AGENT_CONTAINER_PIDS_LIMIT=4096
# AGENT_CONTAINER_CPUS=2
# AGENT_CONTAINER_ENDRUN_SECONDS=30
# AGENT_CONTAINER_IDLE_MINUTES=30
# AGENT_SESSION_IDLE_MINUTES=30

# Optional: a proxy this site reaches model providers through. The model relay
# honours HTTPS_PROXY (a CONNECT tunnel, so provider keys stay inside TLS) and
# NO_PROXY (hosts, domain suffixes, host:port, *; localhost always goes direct),
# and also their lower-case forms. It never sends an http:// provider through a
# proxy, because the proxy would see the key. Credentials may be in the URL.
# HTTPS_PROXY=http://proxy.example:3128
# NO_PROXY=
